    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2XYC9n7jY4gV3tnop2oYDSv)_\n\n## Problem\n`M-x sp-split-leave-parents` failed with \"Autoloading file .../org/org.elc failed to define function sp-split-leave-parents\".\n\n## Cause\nIn `sp-org-base.el`, `(use-package org :bind (:map org-mode-map (\"C-x s t\" . sp-split-leave-parents)))` makes use-package autoload the command from `org`, which does not define it. Until `sp-split-leave-parents.el` is loaded (it is only required by `sp-vulpea-ext`), the stub points at the wrong file.\n\n## Fix\nDeclare `(autoload 'sp-split-leave-parents \"sp-split-leave-parents\" nil t)` before the `use-package org` block. use-package only adds its own autoload when the function is not already bound, so the correct one wins and the key binding is unchanged. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Verification\nNot run in Emacs (none in the sandbox). I read the code only; please check `C-x s t` and `M-x sp-split-leave-parents` in a fresh Emacs. If the error persists, `M-x describe-function sp-split-leave-parents` will show which file the stub names.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ad8QyaD8EpsqigU9Prgkef)_",
